# Growth tracking invariants

## WHO computation
- ALL percentile computation must go through `WhoPercentileService` — never compute inline in controllers
- Percentiles must be stored in the DB at write time — never computed on the fly at read time
- Age must be stored as `age_months_at_recording` (float) at write time from DOB + `recorded_at`

## BLE safety
- BLE reads must ONLY be triggered by explicit user tap (never on mount or background)
- Always validate BLE reading values before saving:
  weight_kg: 0.5–200, height_cm: 30–250, spo2: 50–100, bp_systolic: 50–250
- If a reading is outside valid range, reject with user-facing error — never silently save

## Percentile display rules
- < P3 or > P97: always show red badge — flag prominently
- P3–P15 or P85–P97: amber badge
- P15–P85: green badge
- Always show disclaimer on growth charts: "Consult your doctor for clinical interpretation"

## Data ownership
- A `child_profile` is owned by the patient (parent)
- Doctors can read and add readings but cannot delete child profiles or past readings
